  "title": "Seven new homes in Lahaina historic district",
  "summary": "On September 3, the commission approved the plan for seven single-family homes in a Lahaina historic district, requiring an archaeological monitor for all initial ground-disturbing work. A commissioner noted a known burial on an adjacent lot, and a new consultant will do a new archaeological study, with no ground disturbance until it and a monitoring plan are done. In July, test trenches on the home sites found no burials.",
